{
  "schema": "hollow-star-looks-1",
  "version": "2026-09-25",
  "note": "Presentation only. How non-player figures look: town residents, fixture foes and filler. Nothing here changes a roll, a disposition or a number, and nothing here is canon. Canon roster characters (DM053 and the Divineverse matrix) are deliberately absent: their appearance must be sourced from their owner files before it is authored here.",
  "how_to_extend": {
    "archetypes": "A named look anyone can reuse. `appearance` uses the character creator's own fields and option ids (hollowstar/content/character_creation.json appearance.fields). A value may be an option id, a '#rrggbb' colour (for colour fields: skin_tone, hair_color, eye_color, outfit, cloth_color, accent_color), or a list of either -- a list is picked per figure from a stable seed, so a squad of three reads as three people. `race`, `gender` and `age` ('adult' or 'child') may be fixed or listed the same way. `costume` is presentation-only gear drawn on the figure (rows shaped like an item's `presentation` block: silhouette, material, fx, rarity, handedness, coverage); it never enters mechanics or the item lists. `aura` adds an element glow token (see ELEMENT_COLOUR in web/actor-look.js).",
    "residents": "Resident id (floor_one_life.json) -> {archetype, ...overrides}. Overrides merge over the archetype, appearance field by field.",
    "foes": "Base actor name without its squad number ('Town watch 2' -> 'Town watch') -> {archetype, ...overrides}. Real equipment always wins: costume never replaces an equipped weapon's silhouette.",
    "by_class": "Fallback archetype by resident class when a resident has no entry.",
    "verify": "Open /web/actor-lab.html to see any look, and run tests/test_looks_and_salience.py."
  },
